; Convert a picture pen position to a screen byte address and bit mask
;
; The picture area is 256x128 pixels with y growing upward, so the pixel row
; from the top is $7F-y. Builds the Spectrum screen address of the byte
; holding the pixel (third, character row and pixel line from the row; column
; from x/8) and the mask of the pixel in that byte (bit 7 for x mod 8 = 0).
; Used by the line, plot and fill routines of the picture drawer.
; .
; Hardware: none (computes an address in the screen bitmap only).
;
; D Pen x, 0-255
; E Pen y, 0-127 (0 is the bottom row of the picture area)
; O:HL Screen address of the byte
; O:A Bit mask of the pixel in that byte
@label=PenToScreen
c$81DE LD A,$7F
 $81E0 SUB E            ; pixel row from the top
 $81E1 LD L,A
 $81E2 AND $07
 $81E4 OR $40           ; $40 + pixel line within the character row
 $81E6 LD H,A
 $81E7 LD A,L
 $81E8 AND $C0
 $81EA RRCA             ; row bits 6-7 (the third) to bits 3-4 of H
 $81EB RRCA
 $81EC RRCA
 $81ED OR H
 $81EE LD H,A
 $81EF LD A,L
 $81F0 AND $38          ; row bits 3-5 (character row in the third) to bits 5-7 of L
 $81F2 RLCA
 $81F3 RLCA
 $81F4 LD L,A
 $81F5 LD A,D
 $81F6 RRCA             ; x/8 is the column
 $81F7 RRCA
 $81F8 RRCA
 $81F9 AND $1F
 $81FB OR L
 $81FC LD L,A
 $81FD LD A,D
 $81FE AND $07
 $8200 PUSH BC
 $8201 LD B,A
 $8202 INC B
 $8203 LD A,$01         ; mask: $80 rotated right (x mod 8)+1 times
*$8205 RRC A
 $8207 DJNZ $8205
 $8209 POP BC
 $820A RET
